 34CL c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2014Bi03:                          
 34CL2c  Phys Rev C 89, 024303 (2014).                                          
 34CL c  Compiled by M. Walters and B. Singh (McMaster), Feb 12, 2014           
 34CL c  Edited by B. Singh, Feb 18, 2014 in response to e-mail reply of        
 34CL2c  Feb 17, 2014 from M. Saha Sarkar                                       
 34CL c  {+27}Al+{+12}C|){+34}Cl+|a+n via fusion-evaporation reaction.          
 34CL c  E({+12}C)=40 MeV. Target=0.50 mg/cm{+2} {+27}Al. Measured E|g, I|g,    
 34CL2c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO), |g|g(lin pol), level lifetimes by DSAM,      
 34CL3c  branching ratios using the 14-UD Pelletron accelerator at TIFR in      
 34CL4c  in Mumbai and the INGA array. Deduced levels, J, |p. Comparison with   
 34CL5c  large-basis shell-model calculations.                                  
 34CL cG $DCO(1) is for gate on |DJ=1, dipole transition; DCO(2) for gate on    
 34CL2cG |DJ=2, quadrupole transition. The geometry for DCO values is 90|' and  
 34CL3cG 157|'. Expected values are |?1 when gating transition and measured     
 34CL4cG transition have the same |DJ and multipole character. In polarization  
 34CL5cG measurements, positive value of POL indicates electric multipolarity   
 34CL6cG and negative value magnetic multipole.                                 
 34CL cG RI$Only the statistical uncertainties are given by 2014Bi03. Systematic
 34CL2cG uncertainties are |?5% (arising from efficiency curve and fittings), as
 34CL3cG communicated by M. Saha Sarkar in e-mail reply of Feb 17, 2014         
 34CL cG TI$As communicated by M. Saha Sarkar in e-mail reply of Feb 17, 2014,  
 34CL2cG photon branching ratios listed in table II of 2014Bi03 are separately  
 34CL3cG measured by gating on transition above the level. Only the statistical 
 34CL4cG uncertainties are given in table II. Systematic uncertainties are |?5% 
 34CL5cG (arising from efficiency curve and fittings). In a few cases the       
 34CL6cG branching ratios differ significantly from those deduced from I|g data 
 34CL7cG in authors' table I; the former should be considered more reliable as  
 34CL8cG suggested in email reply of Feb 17 from authors                        
